From: Dmitry Baryshkov <dmitry.baryshkov@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] iommu: qcom_iommu: allow faulting transactions to terminate

Context banks are programmed with SCTLR.CFCFG, which selects the
stall model. A faulting transaction is held pending CB_RESUME, preventing
the micro-MMU from draining and potentially blocking halt and TLBSYNC.

Add a per-instance no_stall flag; leave CFRE and CFIE enabled so faults
continue to be reported. No instance selects the flag in this patch.
Backport MSM8974 series v1 patch09 against this tree's small cfg structure.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Dmitry Baryshkov <dmitry.baryshkov@oss.qualcomm.com>
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260809-msm8974-iommu-upstream-v1-9-87f5cd492560@oss.qualcomm.com
[BlackF1re: adapt to the BFB-only per-instance configuration structure]

Signed-off-by: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c
index 1c1571501..190de5957 100644
--- a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c
@@ -50,6 +50,8 @@ struct qcom_iommu_bfb_reg {
 };
 
 struct qcom_iommu_cfg {
+	/* Faulting transactions must terminate rather than stall. */
+	bool no_stall;
 	const struct qcom_iommu_bfb_reg *bfb;
 	unsigned int num_bfb;
 };
@@ -362,6 +364,9 @@ static int qcom_iommu_init_domain(struct iommu_domain *domain,
 		if (qcom_iommu->short_desc)
 			reg &= ~ARM_SMMU_SCTLR_AFE;
 
+		if (qcom_iommu->cfg && qcom_iommu->cfg->no_stall)
+			reg &= ~ARM_SMMU_SCTLR_CFCFG;
+
 		if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_CPU_BIG_ENDIAN))
 			reg |= ARM_SMMU_SCTLR_E;
 
